:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447782} {:answer/id #uuid "b41a99d3-c4b3-5fc7-a51f-b02c2727d79c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447783}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b41a99d3-c4b3-5fc7-a51f-b02c2727d79c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447783} :answer-field/id #uuid "bdbf6e1a-6a9e-5e00-b37b-25812a12873a" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448931}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "7c34661b-de46-5e42-88de-7fe1ed369bf4" :question/math-academy-id "q-106710" :question/problem "Let $C$ be the set of all polynomials $p(x)$ such that $p(0)<0.$  Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** The zero-polynomial belongs to $C.$\n- **II.** For any $p(x),q(x)\\in C,$ we have $p(x)+q(x)=q(x)+p(x).$\n- **III.** The addition of polynomials in $C$ is associative." :question/worked-solution "Let's verify the statements one by one.\n\n- Statement I is false. The set $C$ contains only polynomials that evaluate to a negative number at $0.$ However, the zero-polynomial is *not* such a polynomial, as it equals $0≮0$ at $0.$ So, $0\\notin C.$\n\n- Statement II is true. Indeed, for any polynomials $p(x),q(x)\\in C,$ we obtain that\n\n$$\np(x)+q(x)=q(x)+p(x)\n$$\n\nsince polynomial addition is commutative.\n\n- Statement III is true. Indeed, for any polynomials $p(x),q(x),r(x)\\in C,$ we obtain that\n\n$$\n[p(x)+q(x)]+r(x)=p(x)+[q(x)+r(x)]\n$$\n\nsince polynomial addition is associative.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186243957 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124589 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "099e7caf-085a-5fd5-ad3d-1ebf189527b7" :knowledge-point/title "Verifying Properties Involving Scalar Multiplication and the Distributive Laws"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3497eda5-52bc-523b-945d-d05f19503f52" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447802} {:answer/id #uuid "44ac635a-4bd5-5229-88e4-cbb7d8e96d5e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447803}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "44ac635a-4bd5-5229-88e4-cbb7d8e96d5e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447803} :answer-field/id #uuid "fdefdd82-0939-5e22-a509-768a1fed2432" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448941} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "25aca01f-34fb-588b-9dbb-c11c047afdea" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447804} {:answer/id #uuid "8d6a09c3-4c87-5a81-b7e3-0d9a6734a797" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447805}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8d6a09c3-4c87-5a81-b7e3-0d9a6734a797" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447805} :answer-field/id #uuid "418778fd-c7f4-5d7f-a3d0-fd03d98de531" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448942} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ed7df062-5ec2-57b4-8536-99b55fed3f21" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447806} {:answer/id #uuid "e0ea89e7-c9f8-55e0-ab34-178df16a57c0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447807}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e0ea89e7-c9f8-55e0-ab34-178df16a57c0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447807} :answer-field/id #uuid "68bf64ae-6cb2-5663-8dc1-b3784f64d81e" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448943}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "43cc36f0-0278-53e6-b346-3f4ef69a0aaa" :question/math-academy-id "q-106812" :question/problem "Let $G$ be the set of functions $f:R\\to R$ such that $f(0)>0.$ Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** For any $f(x)\\in G,$ we have $1\\cdot f(x)=f(x).$\n- **II.** For any $f(x)\\in G$ and $\\alpha ,\\beta \\in R$, we have $(\\alpha -\\beta )f(x)=\\alpha f(x)-\\beta f(x).$\n- **III.** The scalar multiplication of functions in $G$ is associative." :question/worked-solution "Let's examine each of our statements in turn.\n\n- Statement I is true. Indeed, for any $f(x)\\in G$ and for any fixed $x\\in R,$ the result of $f(x)$ is just a real number. Thus,\n\n$$\n(1\\cdot f)(x)=1\\cdot f(x)=f(x).\n$$\n\n- Statement II is true. Indeed, for any $f(x)\\in G$ and for any fixed $x\\in R,$ the result of $f(x)$ is just a real number. Thus, for any $\\alpha ,\\beta \\in R,$ we obtain that\n\n$$\n(\\alpha -\\beta )f(x)=\\alpha f(x)-\\beta f(x).\n$$\n\n- Statement III is true. Indeed, for any $f(x)\\in G$ and for any fixed $x\\in R,$ the result of $f(x)$ is just a real number. Thus, for any $\\alpha ,\\beta \\in R,$ we obtain that\n\n$$\n\\alpha (\\beta f(x))=(\\alpha \\beta )f(x).\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I, II, and III.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186369901 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124484 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "7eb09138-45df-5e6c-87af-772980ff7546" :knowledge-point/title "Verifying Properties Involving Vector Addition"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ddd351f1-32b0-542a-92ab-95f9a87f3a1c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453490} {:answer/id #uuid "d4b49d49-33d2-5666-b395-3b0958b349ae" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453491}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ddd351f1-32b0-542a-92ab-95f9a87f3a1c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453490} :answer-field/id #uuid "20334df8-715c-597a-9335-d72197c17d35" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454495} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a4ec86e3-0b06-5acc-8fd7-8c9f8345e536" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453492} {:answer/id #uuid "88ec95fb-679a-5210-89ac-59d13943115d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453493}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "88ec95fb-679a-5210-89ac-59d13943115d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453493} :answer-field/id #uuid "b6115756-4217-5b2f-8bef-56b706a37a07" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454496} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b1ad8b87-10f1-5c8c-acae-ea0d175d7cab" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453494} {:answer/id #uuid "9dd33e6e-78a5-5c6f-8605-3eefa3645da6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453495}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9dd33e6e-78a5-5c6f-8605-3eefa3645da6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453495} :answer-field/id #uuid "8d221323-cdda-5fd5-bf5d-7b2bfe508d9b" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454497}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "ba8b444b-5956-57db-9cc4-5f6d4e3d8cd5" :question/math-academy-id "q-162390" :question/problem "Let $F$ be the set of all $2\\times 2$ matrices of the form $[\\begin{aligned}a & a \\\\ 0 & a\\end{aligned}],$ where $a\\in R.$ Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** The identity matrix ${I}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]$ belongs to $F.$\n- **II.** For the zero matrix $O$ and any $A\\in F,$ we have $A+O=A.$\n- **III.** For any $A,B\\in F,$ we have $A+B=B+A.$" :question/worked-solution "Let's examine each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement I is false. Indeed, every element $A$ in $F$ satisfies ${a}_{12}={a}_{11}={a}_{22},$ however, for the identity matrix ${I}_{2}$ we have ${i}_{12}=0\\ne {i}_{11}.$\n\n- Statement II is true. Indeed, as for any $2\\times 2$ matrix $A,$ with real entries, we have\n\n$$\nA+O=A.\n$$\n\n- Statement III is true. Indeed, For any matrices $A,B\\in F$ we obtain that \n\n$$\nA+B=B+A\n$$\n\nsince matrix addition is commutative.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186480670 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124484 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "7eb09138-45df-5e6c-87af-772980ff7546" :knowledge-point/title "Verifying Properties Involving Vector Addition"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "48152817-d761-520e-9162-c1b4b1f93594" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186480231} {:answer/id #uuid "712e9086-50d5-5be4-8bd2-838841d9d6bd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186480293} {:answer/id #uuid "83d03ad1-699f-5271-aa16-12a88da19753" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186480330} {:answer/id #uuid "a6e264d4-7eff-58c9-af68-052f1a966bca" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186480388} {:answer/id #uuid "f6333884-91ca-5deb-b697-754d8fa83902" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I, II, and III" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186480515}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f6333884-91ca-5deb-b697-754d8fa83902" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I, II, and III" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186480515} :answer-field/id #uuid "1ca2ea90-b950-5f61-9fa7-e9762d8343dd" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186480542}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "750b7607-258b-55b2-8f3f-8eb360c8a574" :question/math-academy-id "q-94644" :question/problem "Let $V$ be the set of polynomials of the form $a{x}^{2},$ where $a\\in Q.$ Which of the following statements are true? \n\nI. The zero-polynomial belongs to $V.$\n\nII. For the zero-polynomial $0$ and any $p(x)\\in V,$ we have $p(x)+0=p(x).$\n\nIII. For any $p(x),q(x)\\in V,$ we have $p(x)+q(x)=q(x)+p(x).$" :question/worked-solution "Let's examine each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement I is true. Indeed, the zero-polynomial can be represented as\n\n$$\n0=0\\cdot {x}^{2}.\n$$\n\nHence, $0\\in V.$\n\n- Statement II is true. Indeed, for the zero-polynomial $0$ and any $p(x)\\in V,$ we have\n\n$$\np(x)+0=p(x)\n$$\n\nsince $0$ is the unique zero element in the set of all polynomials.\n\n- Statement III is true. Indeed, for any $p(t),q(t)\\in V,$ we obtain that \n\n$$\np(t)+q(t)=q(t)+p(t).\n$$\n\nHence, the addition of polynomials in $V$ is commutative.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I, II, and III.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186360476 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124589 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "099e7caf-085a-5fd5-ad3d-1ebf189527b7" :knowledge-point/title "Verifying Properties Involving Scalar Multiplication and the Distributive Laws"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1474a3e2-e736-5b19-b171-2993227de350" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452041} {:answer/id #uuid "9b98079f-fe90-5caa-80dc-7270db379b3f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452042}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1474a3e2-e736-5b19-b171-2993227de350" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452041} :answer-field/id #uuid "1b953735-6549-5e74-ab38-2ec79639a675" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452868} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "86ec80e9-0df8-5cfd-835c-fd48ded2c328" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452043} {:answer/id #uuid "69a7ca61-3cc1-5e61-baf2-dce127884e9d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452044}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "69a7ca61-3cc1-5e61-baf2-dce127884e9d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452044} :answer-field/id #uuid "6c2d98f2-45aa-5106-9dbe-0b4791dcbb31" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452869} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1b9c42b9-1d20-519c-b18e-c231243717e3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452045} {:answer/id #uuid "d0500db8-c267-5db0-b0d1-5a3a33dc76d8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452046}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d0500db8-c267-5db0-b0d1-5a3a33dc76d8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452046} :answer-field/id #uuid "a50fa798-62df-5307-a327-7013e9729e7e" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452870}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "0778fc80-bc7a-5da8-b455-9670cb2d5afb" :question/math-academy-id "q-94711" :question/problem "Let $L$ be the set of polynomials of the form $ax+b,$ where $a,b\\in R.$ Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** For any $p(x),q(x)\\in L,$ we have $2(p(x)+q(x))=2p(x)-2q(x).$\n- **II.** For any $p(x)\\in L$ and $\\alpha ,\\beta \\in R,$ we have $(\\alpha +\\beta )p(x)=\\alpha p(x)+\\beta p(x).$\n- **III.** For any $p(x)\\in L,$ we have $1\\cdot p(x)=p(x).$" :question/worked-solution "Let's examine each of our statements in turn.\n\n- Statement I is false. For example, consider the polynomials $p(x)=x+1$ and $q(x)=x-1$ from $L.$ Then:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2(p(x)+q(x)) & =2(x+1+x-1) \\\\  & =2(2x) \\\\  & =4x \\\\ 2p(x)-2q(x) & =2(x+1)-2(x-1) \\\\  & =2x+2-2x+2 \\\\  & =4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement II is true. Indeed, for any $p(x)\\in L$ and for any fixed $x\\in R,$ the result of $p(x)$ is just a real number. Thus, for any $\\alpha ,\\beta \\in R,$ we obtain that\n\n$$\n(\\alpha +\\beta )p(x)=\\alpha p(x)+\\beta p(x).\n$$\n\n- Statement III is true. Indeed, for any $p(x)\\in L$ and for any fixed $x\\in R,$ the result of $p(x)$ is just a real number. Thus,\n\n$$\n1\\cdot p(x)=p(x).\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only.\""}]}
